  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 143 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nShowers and thunderstorms are possible tonight into early Tuesday \nmorning as a wave skirts by to the north and west. For early this\nevening, instability grows across central SD, with CAPE values of\n2000-3000 J/kg, but only marginal shear. Initially storms will be\nmost likely west of the area, but some development could creep into\nGregory and Brule counties. Capping may preclude any developmeny,\nso only low confidence in storms actually developing. Later tonight   \ninto early Tuesday morning a tail of convection could build south \ntowards highway 14 and into pars of southwest MN. Here CAPE values\nof about 1000-1500 J/kg will be possible with minor-moderate shear.\nSpome question as the whether we see an increase in moisture around \n800 mb which appears to be needed to produce a few updrafts. Once\nagain this is somewhat lower confidence set up. Isolated severe\nweather will be possible in bth areas, half dollars and 70 mph winds\nin central SD and quarters and 60 mph winds in southwest MN.\n\nWarmer air aloft builds into the area Tuesday, but other than northwest \nIA the threat for showers and thudnerstorms will be fairly low. If \nthere is some elevated moisture there could be a little activity in\nthe morning. Northwest IA may see just enough instability and shear\non Tuesday afternoon for a couple of strong to severe updrafts.\n\nBehind this cooler and drier air builds into the area which appears to \nbring dry and seasonally mild conditions for Wednesday and Thursday.\n\nStronger westerly winds aloft will spread across the area Friday into\nthe weekend. This shoudl bring occasional chances for showers and\nthunderstorms during this time. Friday night appears to be a better\nchance right now. As the warmer conditions and somewhat deeper \ninstability build in Friday night into Saturday isolated severe \nstorms will be possile.",
